# This is the example of ONE Bid Desk. Make three copies from it: .env.bid-desk-alfa, .env.bid-desk-bravo and .env.bid-desk-charlie, each one next to the compose file of its Bid Desk, in /srv/agents/bid-desk-alfa, /srv/agents/bid-desk-bravo and /srv/agents/bid-desk-charlie (RUNBOOK-bid-desk.md, "The env files"). Each copy has mode 600 on the host.
# Each copy holds keys and a token of its own: no key and no token stands in two copies. Fill each copy for its own Bid Desk, with its own supplier key, its own service key, its own token and its own agent record.
# Names, placeholders and published values only: this example holds no key, no secret and no usable token.
# The service and the runtime of a Bid Desk both read its copy, and no other file. A name that the compose file sets wins over this file, so none of those names stands here. Three kinds of line are the exception: the window of the advert, which both sides read, the supplier key line, which the service blanks, and the key line of the service, which the runtime blanks.
# The three lines that name the Bid Desk (BID_DESK_INSTANCE, BID_DESK_ORGANISATION and BID_DESK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN) and the state folder stand in the compose file of each Bid Desk, so that a copy of the wrong env file cannot change the instance. The port stands there too: the runtime has 8080 from its compose file, and the service has the port 9106 of its image. So no PORT line stands here.
# A copy holds two keys and a token. It never enters git: the .gitignore of the repository covers .env.* except *.example.
# A container reads its copy when it is created. After a change, create the container again: restart does not read it (RUNBOOK-bid-desk.md, "The restart rule").
# A value that breaks a rule stops the start of the service, and the error names the variable and never shows the value.
# The supplier key of the runtime of this Bid Desk. The runtime signs its receipts with it, and its wallet sits at SUPPLIER_ADDRESS. The service never holds it: the compose file blanks SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX for the service.
# The service reads the two public lines, SUPPLIER_PKH and SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX, and publishes them in its manifest. SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX is the public key, 64 hex characters. SUPPLIER_PKH is its hash, 56 hex characters.
# All four lines are empty here on purpose. Write each one with a command that prints nothing, and never type a key in a shell (RUNBOOK-bid-desk.md, "The env files"). Each Bid Desk has a supplier key and a wallet of its own.
SUPPLIER_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX=
SUPPLIER_PKH=
SUPPLIER_ADDRESS=
# The service key of this Bid Desk. It is a raw Ed25519 key of 64 lowercase hex characters, and it is a key of its own: the service stops at start when it is the supplier key. It pays for the model hire of each quote and signs the transactions of the janitor, which settles the escrows that a hire leaves behind.
# The variable has the same name in the three copies, and each copy holds a different key. BID_DESK_SERVICE_PKH is its key hash. The line is public and optional. When it has a value, it must be the hash of the key before it, or the service stops at start.
# Both lines are empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without the key. The compose file blanks the key line for the runtime.
BID_DESK_SERVICE_PRIV_KEY_HEX=
BID_DESK_SERVICE_PKH=
# The token between the runtime and the service. The runtime sends this value, as it stands, as the authorization header of every call to the service. The service answers POST / and POST /precheck only to a call that carries it.
# The form is "Bearer <64 hex characters>", with the quotes: the value has a space. Docker Compose takes the quotes off. The runtime and the service of one Bid Desk read this one line, so they hold one value. Each Bid Desk has a token of its own.
# Empty here on purpose: the service stops at start without it, so a step that was forgotten cannot leave a service that answers anyone. The value stays in the copy. Never paste it into a chat or a log.
SERVICE_AUTH_HEADER=""
# The chain. The runtime reads these lines. They hold public values of Vector mainnet: the network, the node, the time of slot 0, and the reference scripts of the legacy escrow and the legacy advert.
# LIVE_CHAIN=1 lets the runtime write to the chain, and the release watcher needs it. Keep ESCROW_REF_UTXO and ADVERT_REF_UTXO while legacy escrows exist.
NETWORK_ID=1
OGMIOS_URL=https://ogmios.vector.mainnet.apexfusion.org
VECTOR_ZERO_TIME_MS=1756485600000
LIVE_CHAIN=1
ESCROW_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#0
ADVERT_REF_UTXO=c8d84c6d67ec67a1efe5e9c6c06d53020e05d1bb96d1c55ecb1eb7d5010c4d54#1
# The identity registry deployment. The lines hold the values that the deployment on Vector mainnet published on 2026-11-03.
# The runtime works an escrow that names the agent with IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, the two scripts IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO and IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO, and AGENT_ID.
# The service reads the four VECTOR_IDENTITY lines for the escrows that it posts and the vault payments that it checks. VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT is the Merkle root of the adoption allowlist, and VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED is the output of the seal of the configuration.
# VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO and VECTOR_IDENTITY_VAULT_REF_UTXO are the reference scripts of the escrow and of the vault. IDENTITY_POLICY_ID must be the policy that the root and the output give, or the service stops at start and names the variables.
IDENTITY_POLICY_ID=d958b823faaa76977d0a07bd9622e87d8e2c85f6692f7f8e8db77762
IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
IDENTITY_ADVERT_REF_UTXO=5efd18a1d90a6b87f1fd4b6fe93acfbe5be082260fd52be194b1088ade7c2758#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_LEGACY_ROOT=e4b6b17ce4a8f83aa17d3181ea140d2bd76c0cfa8a7c44ad69543800b4a0df01
VECTOR_IDENTITY_CONFIG_SEED=6c9856c70b1101f1a4e9ceb373188608013416eff48c51f5bb62706a65d41a2a#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_ESCROW_REF_UTXO=4c2d09858dab0cc22cc77dcb99efed570d909a66e0beb512041dea91005b5e82#0
VECTOR_IDENTITY_VAULT_REF_UTXO=d0bf8f73c915fcbf57ddba714256e520a9a0820bc9e643218db8cf54762d215b#0
# IDENTITY_ADDRESS is the address of the identity registry. Empty means the address of IDENTITY_POLICY_ID, which is right here.
IDENTITY_ADDRESS=
# The record and the advert of this Bid Desk. AGENT_ID is the identifier of the agent record: 64 hex characters, the part of AGENT_DID after did:vector:. ADVERT_REF is the reference of the advert: <transaction hash>#<output index>.
# Both lines are empty here on purpose. The operator posts the advert with the hosted tools after the service runs, and writes both values in the copy of this Bid Desk (RUNBOOK-bid-desk.md, "The start order"). The runtime does not start without ADVERT_REF.
AGENT_ID=
ADVERT_REF=
# The services that the hook, the job and the janitor read. Each line is empty here, and an empty line keeps the default of the code, which is Vector mainnet. Set a line only to use another service.
# VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL is the node, and the code takes an https address only: the janitor reads the tip of the node with it. VECTOR_KOIOS_URL is the indexer of the ledger. VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL takes the transactions.
# VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL is the marketplace indexer, in which the model suppliers are found. IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL is the identity gateway: the hook reads the record of the sender from it, and the job reads the credential of the desk.
# CHECKS_READ_BUDGET_MS is the most that one timed read of the hook may take, in milliseconds: a whole number from 500 to 2249. The hook makes 4 timed reads and the runtime waits 10 seconds for it, so the 4 reads must stay under 9000 ms. Empty keeps 1200.
VECTOR_OGMIOS_URL=
VECTOR_KOIOS_URL=
VECTOR_SUBMIT_URL=
VECTOR_MARKETPLACE_INDEXER_URL=
IDENTITY_GATEWAY_URL=
CHECKS_READ_BUDGET_MS=
# The window of the advert, in milliseconds: 8 minutes. The compose file gives the runtime the same value, and the service does not start with less than 480000.
# The other terms of the advert are constants of the code, so no line stands here for them: the price is 1 unit, 1000000 lovelace, and each bond is 1 unit. The lock of the escrow is the price and both bonds: 3 units. The operator posts the advert with these terms (RUNBOOK-bid-desk.md, "The start order").
ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS=480000
# The manifest. What the service serves at /agent.json is hashed into the advert, so each line that goes into it must be final before the hash is taken: OPERATOR_CONTACT, AGENT_DID, AGENT_VERSION, AGENT_STATUS_CHIP, AGENT_STATUS_SINCE and ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL of this block; ADVERT_MAX_PROCESSING_MS, the window of the advert; IDENTITY_POLICY_ID and IDENTITY_ADDRESS, the identity registry; SUPPLIER_PKH and SUPPLIER_PUB_KEY_HEX, the supplier lines; BID_DESK_SERVICE_PKH, the key hash of the service key; LLM_MODEL_ALLOWLIST and LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE, the model and the price limit of the model hire; and BID_DESK_INSTANCE and BID_DESK_PUBLIC_ORIGIN, the instance lines of the compose file.
# Each Bid Desk has its own manifest and its own hash, because the manifest names the Bid Desk, its agent record, its keys and its price list. A change afterwards means a retired advert and a new one. OPERATOR_CONTACT is required and is published. It is the contact address that the live agents of the operator publish. The operator types it, and no file of the repository holds it.
# AGENT_DID is written when the agent record of this Bid Desk exists: did:vector: and the 64 hex characters of AGENT_ID. It is required, and it names a different agent in each copy.
# AGENT_VERSION stays empty: the service has its own default. AGENT_STATUS_CHIP is proposed, deployed or live, and it stays proposed until the first live run. Empty AGENT_STATUS_SINCE keeps the default date of the code, and a date as YYYY-MM-DD goes with a change of the word.
# ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL stays empty: the transaction of an advert cannot be inside the manifest that the advert hashes.
OPERATOR_CONTACT=<contact address that the live agents publish>
AGENT_DID=
AGENT_VERSION=
AGENT_STATUS_CHIP=proposed
AGENT_STATUS_SINCE=
ADVERT_EXPLORER_URL=
# What the service hires. The first line limits the model hire of the decision: the models, comma separated with no space, in order of preference. LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE is the most that a hire may be priced at, 1000000 lovelace, 1 unit.
# The two bond lines limit the supplier bond and the buyer bond of the model advert. Every such advert has bonds of 1000000, so 2000000 is the limit for each. These are the values of Advocate. All four lines are required, and the service never fills in a limit for you.
LLM_MODEL_ALLOWLIST=deepseek/deepseek-v4-flash
LLM_MAX_PRICE_LOVELACE=1000000
LLM_MAX_SUPPLIER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
LLM_MAX_BUYER_BOND_LOVELACE=2000000
# The fault switch of the service. The line is empty for a clean run. The one value of this agent is quote_off_price_list, and it is for a failure run of one Bid Desk only (RUNBOOK-bid-desk.md, "The fault switch"): any other value stops the start.
# The switch of one Bid Desk never changes another. Every quote carries the member fault_mode. It is the empty text in a clean run, and it is the value of the switch in a failure run.
FAULT_MODE=
